           'summary': 'Microsoft Corp.  has foiled a sophisticated hacking '
                      'plan to disrupt election infrastructure in the U.S., '
                      'the company said Monday. Microsoft said it obtained a '
                      'federal court order to disable the IP addresses '
                      'associated with computer servers behind Trickbot, an '
                      'immense malware network that criminals were using to '
                      'launch cyberattacks. The legal action dovetails with an '
                      'offensive by U.S. Cyber Command to disrupt the '
                      'cybercriminals, according to The Washington Post. '
                      'Microsoft acknowledged the digital intruders are likely '
                      'to revive their operations.',
